<Base title="About" description="Who writes this log and why.">
  <p class="kicker">// about</p>
  <h1>Hi, I'm Nick.</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I run marketing for a company building connected-vehicle safety technology, and I co-founded a growth marketing consultancy on the side. I've spent eight-plus years in technical B2B marketing. I am not a programmer by training.</p>
    <p>Most build logs are written by engineers, for engineers. This one is for people like me: marketers and operators who want to actually build with AI, not just prompt it.</p>
    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <p>Write-ups of things I've built: scheduled agents, memory systems, an MCP server, a desk light that tells me what my agents are doing. Each one covers what worked, what broke, what it cost, and what I'd do differently.</p>
    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>Most of this was built in collaboration with Claude, including a persona assistant I've tuned for day-to-day work. Data-gathering goes to scripts. Judgment and voice stay with people (and occasionally the AI, when it's earned it).</p>
  </div>
</Base>
